\">As of Oct 12, the record on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 7 grids runs 75 years, from 1951 to 2025, and November to December came in under 90% of normal in 38 of them. In 2025 on the middle of the grids, August to September came in at 25% of normal and September to October at 40%. In 2026 so far, March to April came in at 185% of normal on the middle of the grids. Grid 23863 had the driest year on the page, 1988, at 60% of normal.</p>"}
